Current round public responses reinforce the majority position from earlier rounds: a log2FC cut cannot eliminate biological contamination and providing a command-line recipe to hide it is data masking/misconduct. Consensus is that any logFC filter is at best a transparent diagnostic flag for QC reporting, not decontamination. The set should be intersected with curated tumour markers and reported as QC evidence, never used to filter the count matrix or results table before inference.

